contentText:
Mau y Ricky reflect on the people, values and experiences that keep them grounded through life’s constant movement. In partnership with Lincoln, the brothers slow down and recharge to consider what matters most — from family and their bond as brothers to staying connected to themselves and the world around them.

Ricky Montaner&nbsp;

Big brother, let me. I&#8217;ve spent my whole life going from one place to another, and with time you realize that the pause is also part of the journey. It only takes driving to a place like this to slow down the pace and reconnect with what really matters to you.&nbsp;

Mau Montaner&nbsp;

The more life changes, the more you realize how important those habits are that keep my feet on the ground. Those are the moments that always remind me to return to who I am, no matter how fast everything goes. From my parents, I feel they always gave us that feeling of feeling that you were welcome and you were loved, whether things went well for you or if things went so-so for you.

[sings] No matter when, no matter- The guitar has always been for me like my companion with whom I can vent and with whom I can get through any moment in life. [guitar]

When I return to my little house and see the smile of my son and my wife, that for me is

success.&nbsp;

Technology is often a double-edged sword. You need to step away from it to be able to rest, but also sometimes it makes it easier, it makes it easier to downshift, right? [soft music] When I&#8217;m alone in the car, often that&#8217;s my moment to recharge. It&#8217;s also a moment where ideas start to flow. Apart from my family, I protect our creative time a lot.

